  "style": "Command labels use the noun form (열기, 저장, 내보내기); messages use the formal 합니다/하십시오 style and avoid a second-person pronoun. Spacing follows Korean orthography and Microsoft Korean UI usage (도구 모음, 대화 상자). A command that opens a dialog keeps the trailing … as in English. Sentences use half-width punctuation (. , : ?) with no full stop in labels. Menu paths are written 파일 ▸ 열기 with a space either side of ▸. Key names (Ctrl, Shift, Alt, Esc, F1) stay in Latin letters as they are."
